+##### How sensitive is the deposit to the interest rate?
 
+These six payments are fixed and known, so the PV of `r format(round(present_val, 2), nsmall = 2)` is an exact number rather than an estimate. There is no sample to bootstrap and nothing to test: resampling the payments with replacement (as an earlier version did) shuffles which amount is paid when and doesn't describe any real uncertainty.
 
+What *is* uncertain is the interest rate you will actually earn. Below, the rate is assumed to be normally distributed around 2.14% with a standard deviation of 0.5% (an illustrative assumption), and we look at how the required deposit varies and how likely a round $20,000 deposit is to be enough.
 
 ```{r}
