+probabilities (qx) at various ages, the likelihood that someone aged x
+dies before x + 1. Survival probabilities are their complement, px = 1 -
+qx. Both are derived from historical mortality data. Statistical
+inference techniques are employed to analyze and interpret these
+probabilities, including:</p>
