 <div id="hypothesis-testing-on-mortality-rates" class="section level4">
 <h4>Hypothesis Testing on Mortality Rates</h4>
-<p>We can perform a hypothesis test to determine if the mortality rate
-at age 50 has significantly changed between 1921 and 2021.</p>
-<div class="sourceCode" id="cb70"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb70-1"><a href="#cb70-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># Hypothesis testing for mortality rates at age 50</span></span>
-<span id="cb70-2"><a href="#cb70-2" tabindex="-1"></a>row_1921 <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">subset</span>(life_table, Year <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">1921</span> <span class="sc">&amp;</span> Age <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">50</span>)</span>
-<span id="cb70-3"><a href="#cb70-3" tabindex="-1"></a>row_2021 <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">subset</span>(life_table, Year <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">2021</span> <span class="sc">&amp;</span> Age <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">50</span>)</span>
-<span id="cb70-4"><a href="#cb70-4" tabindex="-1"></a>mort_1921 <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> row_1921<span class="sc">$</span>qx</span>
-<span id="cb70-5"><a href="#cb70-5" tabindex="-1"></a>mort_2021 <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> row_2021<span class="sc">$</span>qx</span>
-<span id="cb70-6"><a href="#cb70-6" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># two-proportion z-test using each year&#39;s survivors at age 50 as the sample size</span></span>
-<span id="cb70-7"><a href="#cb70-7" tabindex="-1"></a>se <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">sqrt</span>(mort_1921 <span class="sc">*</span> (<span class="dv">1</span> <span class="sc">-</span> mort_1921) <span class="sc">/</span> row_1921<span class="sc">$</span>lx <span class="sc">+</span> mort_2021 <span class="sc">*</span> (<span class="dv">1</span> <span class="sc">-</span> mort_2021) <span class="sc">/</span> row_2021<span class="sc">$</span>lx)</span>
-<span id="cb70-8"><a href="#cb70-8" tabindex="-1"></a>t_stat <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> (mort_2021 <span class="sc">-</span> mort_1921) <span class="sc">/</span> se</span>
-<span id="cb70-9"><a href="#cb70-9" tabindex="-1"></a>p_value <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="dv">2</span> <span class="sc">*</span> <span class="fu">pnorm</span>(<span class="sc">-</span><span class="fu">abs</span>(t_stat))</span>
-<span id="cb70-10"><a href="#cb70-10" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;T-statistic:&quot;</span>, t_stat, <span class="st">&quot;</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
-<pre><code>## T-statistic: -17.85743</code></pre>
-<div class="sourceCode" id="cb72"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb72-1"><a href="#cb72-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;P-value:&quot;</span>, p_value, <span class="st">&quot;</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
+<p>We can perform a two-proportion z-test to check whether the mortality
+rate at age 50 changed between 1921 and 2021. One caveat: a life table’s
+lx counts survivors out of a hypothetical 100,000 births, not the real
+population, so using it as the sample size makes this an illustration. A
+proper test would use the actual death counts and exposures (the HMD
+<code>Deaths_1x1</code> and <code>Exposures_1x1</code> files).</p>
+<div class="sourceCode" id="cb63"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb63-1"><a href="#cb63-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># Hypothesis testing for mortality rates at age 50</span></span>
+<span id="cb63-2"><a href="#cb63-2" tabindex="-1"></a>row_1921 <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">subset</span>(life_table, Year <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">1921</span> <span class="sc">&amp;</span> Age <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">50</span>)</span>
+<span id="cb63-3"><a href="#cb63-3" tabindex="-1"></a>row_2021 <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">subset</span>(life_table, Year <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">2021</span> <span class="sc">&amp;</span> Age <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">50</span>)</span>
+<span id="cb63-4"><a href="#cb63-4" tabindex="-1"></a>mort_1921 <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> row_1921<span class="sc">$</span>qx</span>
+<span id="cb63-5"><a href="#cb63-5" tabindex="-1"></a>mort_2021 <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> row_2021<span class="sc">$</span>qx</span>
+<span id="cb63-6"><a href="#cb63-6" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="co"># two-proportion z-test using each year&#39;s survivors at age 50 as the sample size</span></span>
+<span id="cb63-7"><a href="#cb63-7" tabindex="-1"></a>se <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">sqrt</span>(mort_1921 <span class="sc">*</span> (<span class="dv">1</span> <span class="sc">-</span> mort_1921) <span class="sc">/</span> row_1921<span class="sc">$</span>lx <span class="sc">+</span> mort_2021 <span class="sc">*</span> (<span class="dv">1</span> <span class="sc">-</span> mort_2021) <span class="sc">/</span> row_2021<span class="sc">$</span>lx)</span>
+<span id="cb63-8"><a href="#cb63-8" tabindex="-1"></a>t_stat <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> (mort_2021 <span class="sc">-</span> mort_1921) <span class="sc">/</span> se</span>
+<span id="cb63-9"><a href="#cb63-9" tabindex="-1"></a>p_value <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="dv">2</span> <span class="sc">*</span> <span class="fu">pnorm</span>(<span class="sc">-</span><span class="fu">abs</span>(t_stat))</span>
+<span id="cb63-10"><a href="#cb63-10" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;q50 in 1921:&quot;</span>, mort_1921, <span class="st">&quot;  q50 in 2021:&quot;</span>, mort_2021, <span class="st">&quot;</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
+<pre><code>## q50 in 1921: 0.01016   q50 in 2021: 0.00275</code></pre>
+<div class="sourceCode" id="cb65"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb65-1"><a href="#cb65-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;z-statistic:&quot;</span>, t_stat, <span class="st">&quot;</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
+<pre><code>## z-statistic: -17.85743</code></pre>
+<div class="sourceCode" id="cb67"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb67-1"><a href="#cb67-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;P-value:&quot;</span>, p_value, <span class="st">&quot;</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
 <pre><code>## P-value: 2.530244e-71</code></pre>
-<div class="sourceCode" id="cb74"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb74-1"><a href="#cb74-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="cf">if</span> (p_value <span class="sc">&lt;</span> <span class="fl">0.05</span>) {</span>
-<span id="cb74-2"><a href="#cb74-2" tabindex="-1"></a>  <span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;We reject the null hypothesis that the mortality rate at age 50 has not changed between 1921 and 2021</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span>)</span>
