+class="section level5">
+<h5>How sensitive is the deposit to the interest rate?</h5>
+<p>These six payments are fixed and known, so the PV of 19800.98 is an
+exact number rather than an estimate. There is no sample to bootstrap
+and nothing to test: resampling the payments with replacement (as an
+earlier version did) shuffles which amount is paid when and doesn’t
+describe any real uncertainty.</p>
+<p>What <em>is</em> uncertain is the interest rate you will actually
+earn. Below, the rate is assumed to be normally distributed around 2.14%
+with a standard deviation of 0.5% (an illustrative assumption), and we
+look at how the required deposit varies and how likely a round $20,000
+deposit is to be enough.</p>
