+<div id="what-interest-rate-would-reach-25000" class="section level4">
+<h4>What interest rate would reach $25,000?</h4>
+<p>As with the PV, the AV is an exact number once the rate is fixed, so
+a bootstrap interval or hypothesis test around it isn’t meaningful. A
+more useful question is what rate you would need for the savings to
+reach a target, say $25,000 at t = 6.</p>
+<div class="sourceCode" id="cb34"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb34-1"><a href="#cb34-1" tabindex="-1"></a>target_av <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="dv">25000</span></span>
+<span id="cb34-2"><a href="#cb34-2" tabindex="-1"></a>av_at <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="cf">function</span>(r) <span class="fu">sum</span>(cash_flows <span class="sc">*</span> (<span class="dv">1</span> <span class="sc">+</span> r) <span class="sc">^</span> (<span class="dv">6</span> <span class="sc">-</span> <span class="dv">0</span><span class="sc">:</span><span class="dv">5</span>))</span>
+<span id="cb34-3"><a href="#cb34-3" tabindex="-1"></a>required_rate <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">uniroot</span>(<span class="cf">function</span>(r) <span class="fu">av_at</span>(r) <span class="sc">-</span> target_av, <span class="fu">c</span>(<span class="dv">0</span>, <span class="fl">0.5</span>))<span class="sc">$</span>root</span>
+<span id="cb34-4"><a href="#cb34-4" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;Interest rate needed for an AV of $25,000:&quot;</span>, <span class="fu">round</span>(<span class="dv">100</span> <span class="sc">*</span> required_rate, <span class="dv">3</span>), <span class="st">&quot;%</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
+<pre><code>## Interest rate needed for an AV of $25,000: 5.47 %</code></pre>
+<div class="sourceCode" id="cb36"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb36-1"><a href="#cb36-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;Check: AV at that rate =&quot;</span>, <span class="fu">round</span>(<span class="fu">av_at</span>(required_rate), <span class="dv">2</span>))</span></code></pre></div>
+<pre><code>## Check: AV at that rate = 24999.85</code></pre>
+<p>You would need about 5.47% a year, compared with the 2.14%
+assumed.</p>
