+<h4>Monthly Payments Under Interest-Rate Uncertainty</h4>
+<p>Once the loan is signed the payment is fixed, but before you lock in
+a rate you don’t know exactly what you’ll be offered. Assuming the rate
+you’re offered is normally distributed around 2.88% with a standard
+deviation of 0.25% (an illustrative assumption), we can simulate the
+range of monthly payments.</p>
