+<div id="life-expectancy-at-birth-over-time" class="section level4">
+<h4>Life Expectancy at Birth Over Time</h4>
+<p>Each year has exactly one life expectancy at birth, calculated from
+that year’s mortality rates, so these are not repeated samples of one
+quantity. Averaging them, or bootstrapping them as an earlier version
+did, mixes a century of very different conditions into a single number
+that doesn’t describe any real population. It is more informative to
+look at the trend.</p>
+<div class="sourceCode" id="cb72"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb72-1"><a href="#cb72-1" tabindex="-1"></a>e0 <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">subset</span>(life_table, Age <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">0</span>)</span>
+<span id="cb72-2"><a href="#cb72-2" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">plot</span>(e0<span class="sc">$</span>Year, e0<span class="sc">$</span>ex, <span class="at">type =</span> <span class="st">&quot;l&quot;</span>, <span class="at">lwd =</span> <span class="dv">2</span>, <span class="at">col =</span> <span class="st">&quot;darkgreen&quot;</span>,</span>
+<span id="cb72-3"><a href="#cb72-3" tabindex="-1"></a>     <span class="at">xlab =</span> <span class="st">&quot;Year&quot;</span>, <span class="at">ylab =</span> <span class="fu">expression</span>(e[<span class="dv">0</span>]), <span class="at">main =</span> <span class="st">&quot;Life expectancy at birth (Canada, both sexes)&quot;</span>)</span>
+<span id="cb72-4"><a href="#cb72-4" tabindex="-1"></a>trend <span class="ot">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu">lm</span>(ex <span class="sc">~</span> Year, <span class="at">data =</span> e0)</span>
+<span id="cb72-5"><a href="#cb72-5" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">abline</span>(trend, <span class="at">lty =</span> <span class="dv">2</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
+<p><img src="figures/unnamed-chunk-20-1.png" width="672" /></p>
+<div class="sourceCode" id="cb73"><pre class="sourceCode r"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb73-1"><a href="#cb73-1" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="fu">cat</span>(<span class="st">&quot;Life expectancy at birth: 1921 =&quot;</span>, e0<span class="sc">$</span>ex[e0<span class="sc">$</span>Year <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">1921</span>], <span class="st">&quot;  2021 =&quot;</span>, e0<span class="sc">$</span>ex[e0<span class="sc">$</span>Year <span class="sc">==</span> <span class="dv">2021</span>], <span class="st">&quot;</span><span class="sc">\n</span><span class="st">&quot;</span>)</span></code></pre></div>
