@@ -2864,24 +2832,28 @@ class="section level4">
 <span style="color:blue;">Explanation of Kaplan-Meier Estimator for
 Survival Probabilities</span>
 </summary>
-This code uses the Kaplan-Meier estimator to calculate the survival
-probabilities based on the life table data. The Kaplan-Meier estimator
-is a non-parametric statistic used to estimate the survival function
-from lifetime data. It plots the probability of survival at different
-ages.
+The Kaplan-Meier estimator works on individual lifetimes. A life table
+row is not a person: it says that dx of the 100,000 people died at age
+x. So we expand the 2021 table into deaths at each age, weighted by dx,
+and fit Kaplan-Meier to that. Because no one is censored, the estimate
+should reproduce the life table’s own survival curve, lx / 100,000,
+which makes a good check.
 </details>
