+<p>The Cox model says that, averaged over ages, the risk of death in
+2021 was about 58% lower than in 1951. The second chart shows why this
+should be read with care: the actual ratio isn’t constant. Mortality
+fell by about 90% in childhood, by roughly 35-60% at adult ages, and by
+only about 25% at age 100, so the proportional-hazards assumption
+doesn’t hold well here. A single hazard ratio is a summary, not a rule
+for every age.</p>
